==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|pe}}

===Etymology===
Derives from the name of the Baltic god of thunder, compare Lithuanian [[Perkūnas]]. The meaning was changed to devil by Swedish priests.

===Noun===
'''perkele'''

# The [[Devil]], [[Satan]]
# [[devil]]

====Synonyms====
*[[paholainen]]
*[[piru]]

===Interjection===
'''perkele!'''

# {{vulgar|lang=fi}} an interjection said by someone for example annoyed or surprised
#:''perkele se on hidas!'' (damn it's slow!)

===Adjective===
'''perkele'''

# {{vulgar|lang=fi}} an [[intensifier]]
#:''se on perkeleen ruma'' (it is damn ugly)

